The drawings are not necessarily to scale and may be illustrated by phantom lines, diagrammatic representations, and fragmentary views. In certain instances, details that are not necessary for an understanding of the embodiments or that render other details difficult to perceive may have been omitted.

claims:
1. An apparatus for generating obfuscated data within a computing environment, the apparatus comprising:
at least a processor; and
a memory communicatively connected to the at least a processor, wherein the memory contains instructions configuring the at least a processor to:
access a database containing a plurality of data elements belonging to at least a record;
generate, using a machine-learning model, a set of obfuscated data elements, representative of the at least a record, as a function of the plurality of data elements;
determine a distance measure between at least an obfuscated data element within the set of obfuscated data elements and at least a data element of the plurality of data elements within the database; and
verify, for the at least an obfuscated data element within the set of obfuscated data elements, the distance measure is within a distance range;
cluster the plurality of data elements within the data-base into a plurality of clusters using at least a clustering algorithm; and
select a subset of obfuscated data elements from the set of obfuscated data elements as a function of both the plurality of clusters and the verification.
